{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Keeps</b> — If trouble comes upon those who fear Him, He rescues them; but His loved ones — He keeps them, so that no evil comes upon them." "<b>And all the wicked He will destroy</b> — at the end, for their end is destruction. An earthly king cannot destroy the wicked of his land — perhaps they will conspire against him; therefore he fears them, or he does not recognize them, for he does not know hidden things, and what is finished is as it began."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 145, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:53.337183693Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}